# Keep the data the generators read, and the SQL they emit, at LF in every working
# tree. Without this, git's autocrlf rewrites them on checkout and two things break
# on Windows: a TSV's last column keeps a trailing \r (see the tsv() note in
# scripts/generate-foi-bestiary.ts — silently wrong output, not an error), and a
# regenerated migration differs from the committed one by line endings alone, which
# makes the "don't overwrite an applied migration" guard cry wolf on every run.
scripts/foi/*.tsv           text eol=lf
scripts/foi/*.json          text eol=lf
supabase/migrations/*.sql   text eol=lf
